{number: 68}
{title: Just As I Am, without One Plea}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Just as I am, without one plea,
But that Thy [Bb7] blood was shed for [Eb] me,
And that Thou [Ab] bidd'st me come to Thee,
O Lamb of [Eb] God, I [Bb7] come, I [Eb] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Eb] Just as I am, and waiting not
To rid my [Bb7] soul of one dark [Eb] blot,
To Thee whose [Ab] blood can cleanse each spot,
O Lamb of [Eb] God, I [Bb7] come, I [Eb] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Eb] Just as I am, though tossed about
With many a [Bb7] conflict, many a [Eb] doubt,
Fightings and [Ab] fears within, without,
O Lamb of [Eb] God, I [Bb7] come, I [Eb] come.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[Eb] Just as I am, Thou wilt receive,
Wilt welcome, [Bb7] pardon, cleanse, re-[Eb] lieve;
Because Thy [Ab] promise I believe,
O Lamb of [Eb] God, I [Bb7] come, I [Eb] come.
{end_of_verse}
